# Backend-only advisors data: the cleartext is private and must never be
# committed to this public repo. Only the encrypted advisors.json.enc is
# tracked (see scripts/tools/advisors_crypto.py).
data/processed/advisors.json

# The full enriched dataset (~11 MB), written by generate_static_data.py for
# offline analysis only. Nothing in the pipeline reads it — the CLI bundle is
# built from the same run's in-memory records — and committing it on every data
# run was most of the repository's growth. Run the generator locally for a copy.
data/output/mergers.json

# CLI build intermediates. The bundle is rebuilt by generate_static_data.py
# (scripts/generate/cli_bundle.py) on every run and fed to build_cli_sqlite.py
# in the same job to produce the cli.sqlite that ships on the orphan `cli-dist`
# branch. Nothing reads a committed copy. cli-merger-manifest.json backs a
# not-yet-implemented per-record sync path and has no reader either.
#
# cli-manifest.json IS still tracked: cli_bundle.py reads its `version` and
# `bundle_sha256` to decide whether the bundle changed and what version to
# stamp next. Without it every run would look changed and reset to v1.
data/output/cli/cli-bundle.json
data/output/cli/cli-merger-manifest.json

# Scraper working artifact: the paginated register index is re-fetched fresh at
# the start of every scrape run and only used within that run to derive matter
# links. It changes on every fetch (session token / ordering) even when no
# merger data has changed, so committing it just adds noise.
data/raw/acquisitions-register.html

# Wrangler local state (Cloudflare Pages at the repo root, plus every Worker
# under workers/). Regenerated by `wrangler dev`/`deploy`.
.wrangler/
